Z||000001||Oreif||05-02-2000||10:16 AM||||These are the specs I got from when I had my car redone 2 weeks ago. I went to a brand new goodyear place and the machine they had was only 6 months old.<P>Front<BR>Caster = min 3 max 7<BR>Camber = min -0.3 max 1.3<BR>Toe L or R = min 0.05 max 0.25<BR>Total Toe = min 0.15 max 0.5<P>Rear<BR>Camber = min -1.5 max -0.5<BR>Toe L or R = min -0.1 max 0.1<BR>Total Toe = min -0.2 max 0.2<BR>Thrust angle = min -0.5 max 0.5<P>All numbers in degrees.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-02-2000||10:22 AM||||Oreifs numbers look good, and they include the GM changes made in the TSB I listed in the other thread.<P>Personally I won't use a shop without a working printer on the alignment machine. If they can't give me before and after prints I won't got there. (With the exception of a couple shops I know well anyways....)<P>||||reg||1
